    "proof": [
      "pick_best returns exactly min(left,right) under the lexicographic unsigned key (distance, local ID). A minimum over a total order is associative, commutative and idempotent, so any balanced-tree parenthesization equals the minimum of all 16 leaves.",
      "The old M405 recurrence starts at distance 31 and updates only on a strictly smaller distance. Every legal Hamming distance is 0..16, so center zero is accepted first and every equal-distance tie retains the first, hence lowest, local ID. It computes the same tuple minimum as M414.",
      "Pass zero maps local IDs to global 0..15 and pass one maps local IDs to global 16..31. M414 selects pass one only for strictly lower distance; equality retains pass zero, which is necessarily the lower global ID.",
      "A pass-zero distance of zero cannot be improved by pass one, so zero-stop is globally exact. Population below two deliberately runs q16/pass zero only in both M405 and M414, matching the sealed M410r2 runtime contract."
    ],
